id: banking
name: Retail banking - accounts and payments
industry: Banking & financial services
domain: Retail banking: customers, accounts, cards and payments
scope: Customers and KYC, deposit accounts, cards, payment transactions between accounts, channels and branches, standing instructions, fraud alerts and complaints.
summary: Describes a retail bank's customers, the accounts and cards they hold, and the payments that move money between accounts through channels. A starter model for customer-360, payments analytics and regulatory reporting.
purpose: Common vocabulary for core banking, payments and channel systems; basis for a customer and transaction knowledge graph.
read: A Customer holds Accounts of an Account product at a Branch. Cards are issued on accounts. A Payment transaction debits one account and credits another, is initiated through a Channel and may be a card transaction at a Merchant. Standing instructions and Mandates automate payments; Alerts and Complaints record exceptions.
in: Customers and KYC; Accounts, products and balances; Cards; Payments and channels; Alerts and complaints
out: Lending (see the lending ontology); Treasury and markets; General ledger
std: fibo | high | Accounts, legal entities and financial products follow FIBO Foundations and Business Entities. | Account, LegalEntity, FinancialProduct, FinancialInstitution
std: iso20022 | high | Payment transactions, parties and cash accounts follow the ISO 20022 business model. | Payment, CashAccount, Party, FinancialInstitution, PaymentInstruction
std: lei | low | Corporate customers can carry a Legal Entity Identifier. | LegalEntityIdentifier
std: schema | low | People and organisations are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Person, schema:Organization, schema:BankAccount
== Customer | Customers | Who the bank serves and how it knows them.
Customer | A person or organisation that has, or is applying for, a relationship with the bank.
  - customer number : string !
  - name : string !
  - onboarded on : date
  - risk rating : string
  > has segment > CustomerSegment ?
  > has kyc record > KycRecord *
  > home branch > Branch ?
RetailCustomer : Customer | An individual customer. | ~schema:Person
  - date of birth : date
  - occupation : string
CorporateCustomer : Customer | A company or other legal entity as customer. | ~schema:Organization
  - legal entity identifier : string
  - industry : string
CustomerSegment | A marketing or service grouping of customers.
  * Mass, Affluent, Private, Small business, Corporate
KycRecord | Evidence that the customer's identity and address were verified.
  - document type : string !
  - document number : string
  - verified on : date
  - valid until : date
Branch | A physical office of the bank.
  - branch code : string !
  - city : string
  - region : string
== Account | Accounts and cards | What customers hold.
Account | A record of money held by the bank for a customer, with a balance. | ~schema:BankAccount
  - account number : string !
  - opened on : date !
  - currency : string !
  - current balance : decimal
  - closed on : date
  > held by > Customer + | The owner or joint owners. | holds
  > of product > AccountProduct 1
  > maintained at > Branch 1
  > has status > AccountStatus 1
SavingsAccount : Account | An interest-bearing account for individuals.
  - interest rate percent : decimal
CurrentAccount : Account | A transactional account, usually for businesses, that may allow overdraft.
  - overdraft limit : decimal
TermDeposit : Account | Money placed for a fixed period at a fixed rate.
  - principal : decimal !
  - matures on : date !
  - interest rate percent : decimal
AccountProduct | A type of account the bank offers.
  - product code : string !
  - product name : string !
  - minimum balance : decimal
AccountStatus | The operating state of an account.
  * Active, Dormant, Frozen, Closed
Card | A payment card issued on an account.
  - masked number : string !
  - expires on : date
  - blocked : boolean
  > issued on > Account 1
  > of type > CardType 1
CardType | The kind of card.
  * Debit, Credit, Prepaid
== Payment | Payments | Money moving between accounts.
PaymentTransaction | A movement of money that debits one account and credits another.
  - transaction reference : string !
  - booked at : dateTime !
  - amount : decimal !
  - currency : string !
  - narration : string
  > debits > Account ? | The account money leaves. | debited by
  > credits > Account ? | The account money arrives in. | credited by
  > through channel > Channel 1
  > of type > PaymentType 1
  > has status > PaymentStatus 1
  > to beneficiary > Beneficiary ?
CardTransaction : PaymentTransaction | A payment made with a card at a merchant or ATM.
  - authorisation code : string
  > uses card > Card 1
  > at merchant > Merchant ?
PaymentType | The scheme or instrument used.
  * UPI, NEFT, RTGS, IMPS, Card, Cheque, Cash, Internal transfer
PaymentStatus | The outcome of a payment.
  * Initiated, Completed, Failed, Reversed
Channel | The route through which a customer transacts.
  * Branch, ATM, Internet banking, Mobile app, Point of sale, Call centre
Beneficiary | A payee a customer has registered for outgoing payments.
  - beneficiary name : string !
  - account number : string
  - bank code : string
  > registered by > Customer 1
Merchant | A business that accepts card payments.
  - merchant id : string !
  - merchant name : string
  - category code : string
StandingInstruction | A customer's order to pay a fixed amount at a regular interval.
  - amount : decimal !
  - frequency : string !
  - next run on : date
  > from account > Account 1
  > to beneficiary > Beneficiary 1
== Care | Alerts and complaints | Exceptions and service.
FraudAlert | A signal that a transaction or account may be fraudulent.
  - raised at : dateTime !
  - rule name : string
  - confirmed fraud : boolean
  > on transaction > PaymentTransaction ?
  > on account > Account ?
Complaint | A grievance raised by a customer.
  - reference : string !
  - raised on : date !
  - category : string
  - resolved on : date
  > raised by > Customer 1
  > about transaction > PaymentTransaction ?
rule: constraint | Two sides | A completed payment transaction debits or credits at least one account held at the bank. | PaymentTransaction
rule: constraint | No debit on frozen accounts | A payment cannot debit an account whose status is Frozen or Closed. | PaymentTransaction, Account
rule: constraint | KYC before account | An account can only be opened for a customer with a verified KYC record. | Account, KycRecord
rule: disjoint | Retail or corporate | A customer is either a retail or a corporate customer. | RetailCustomer, CorporateCustomer
uc: Dormant accounts with balance | Branch manager | Which accounts are dormant but hold a balance above a threshold, by branch? | Account, AccountStatus, Branch | Account.has status, Account.current balance, maintained at
uc: Failed payments by channel | Payments operations | What share of payments fail on each channel and payment type? | PaymentTransaction, Channel, PaymentType, PaymentStatus | through channel, PaymentTransaction.of type, PaymentTransaction.has status
uc: Customer 360 | Relationship manager | Show everything a customer holds: accounts, cards, standing instructions and open complaints. | Customer, Account, Card, StandingInstruction, Complaint | holds, issued on, from account, raised by
